2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2474) 'Does every marker we paint scan dead on, with the camera square on and nothing in the way?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2474  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2474) 'Today the gate fails: 276 of 280 visible markers read (98.57%) with the original ids, 278 of 280 (99.29%) with the ids moved. Camera 74 fails with two different ids at the same spot, so that is a position fault: a sharply tilted surface strip sits beside the marker. Ids 664, 703, 1973 and 1268 fail only at some positions, so those are pattern faults, not position faults.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2474  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2474) 'Run the full pass over all 2,600 placed positions once it finishes rendering, and read the gate against that pass: 100% of the markers left after dropping the failing ids must read.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2474  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2474) 'Suit markers: dead-on gate must read every marker
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2474  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2474) 'Drop every marker id that fails the dead-on gate (held in `DROP_IDS`) and require a 100% read rate on the rest. A dropped id's slot stays a hole on the garment rather than being refilled by a neighbour, so the drop list is stable across renders. Camera 74's failure is tracked and fixed separately as a position fault, since it is a tilt problem in the surface strip, not a marker pattern problem, and fixing it is out of this gate's scope.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2474  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2474) 'The two fault classes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2474  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2474) '- Position fault: a marker's own pattern is fine, but where it sits (near a seam, a sharp fold, or a tilted strip) keeps the camera from reading it. Camera 74's dual-id read at one spot is this class.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2474  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2474) '- Pattern fault: the marker's pattern itself does not read cleanly regardless of where it sits. Ids 664, 703, 1973 and 1268, which fail only at some positions and not others, land here once position is ruled out.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2474  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2474) 'Where the code lands
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2474  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2474) '`dead_on.py` scores each rendered position against the expected id, and `texture_markers.py` paints the marker set onto the garment texture before render. Both are referenced from pull requests V-Sekai-fire/interactor-taskweft-persona#6 and #7 against https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/interactor-garment-proxy.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2474  1 LINE
 Text:Written

